WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.400
Previously known for starring in FX's hit
Atlanta, Zazie Beetz was as surprised as anyone

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.950
when she landed the role of super-lucky mutant
Domino in Deadpool 2.

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:13.800
USA Today called her a "captivating standout",
and Vanity Fair proclaimed her "the best thing"

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.320
about the R-rated sequel.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.949
She slipped into the role like she was born
to play it, but getting to that point required

00:00:18.949 --> 00:00:19.960
a lot of hard work.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:22.500
Here's how Beetz got ripped for Deadpool 2.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.609
"I am naturally not one to 'gym'."

00:00:27.609 --> 00:00:29.999
A first time for everything

00:00:29.999 --> 00:00:34.240
Beetz never had to work out for her roles
in 2017's Geostorm, or Atlanta, either.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:38.010
But when she signed on to play Domino, she
knew it was going to require her to hit the

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.010
gym.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:40.010
She told The Hollywood Reporter,

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:43.100
"In my routine day-to-day, I didn't really
work out that much.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.719
So it was a huge transition emotionally and
physically.

00:00:45.719 --> 00:00:47.789
[...] [I'd] never really brought myself that
far."

00:00:47.789 --> 00:00:51.129
And she revealed it wasn't just physically
exhausting, telling Shadow and Act,

00:00:51.129 --> 00:00:55.690
"The training ends up becoming this mental
and emotional experience as well."

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:57.469
Putting in the time

00:00:57.469 --> 00:01:00.449
Beetz trained four hours a day for months,
to get into shape.

00:01:00.449 --> 00:01:02.379
Before filming began, she told IBT,

00:01:02.379 --> 00:01:07.160
"I'm going to be shooting guns, I fight and
a lot of that movement is full body and physical.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:10.610
You're doing that for 12 hours a day and they
just want you to have the stamina."

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:15.080
Reflecting on the fatal on-set accident of
her stunt woman Joi Harris, Beetz also revealed

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:18.960
that leading man Ryan Reynolds helped her
stay focused, telling Entertainment Tonight,

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.740
"It's amazing kind of watching Ryan do his
thing.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:27.580
He's genuinely, incredibly talented."

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.900
Trainer to the stars

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:33.360
You might not know Don Saladino by name, but
you've definitely seen his work.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:37.740
Dubbed "The Superhero Trainer", Saladino's
client list includes Marvel stars Scarlett

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:41.500
Johansson and Sebastian Stan, and Wolverine's
Hugh Jackman.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.060
He's also trained Ryan Reynolds and his wife
Blake Lively.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:49.600
Saladino began training Reynolds for Deadpool
2 in February 2017, which was how he became

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:53.530
acquainted with Beetz, who admitted that she
loved working with Saladino, and the feeling

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:55.970
was very much mutual.

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:57.550
Becoming a superhero

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:02.200
After Deadpool 2 hit theaters, Saladino revealed
to PopSugar, that his first thought when training

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:03.200
Beetz was:

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.170
"We had to turn her into more of an ass kicker."

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:09.280
Saladino admitted that the style of training
he recommended for Beetz can intimidate female

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:10.340
clients, but he said,

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:14.590
"Picking up things like kettlebells and doing
things like squats and split squats — it's

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:16.300
the stuff that works the best.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:20.490
It elevates the heart rate the most, and it's
not linear and so one-dimensional like how

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:22.620
most people train."

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.600
Eating a vegan diet

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:28.950
Because Beetz is vegan, her diet didn't really
change all that much during her Deadpool 2

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:30.580
training, but she told Shadow and Act,

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:34.190
"You have to change how you eat, and it also
takes away your energy.

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:37.911
[...] Doing that alongside shooting and prepping
and all that stuff, it's a lot of work, but

00:02:37.911 --> 00:02:40.050
it was also really cool."

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:41.050
Crushing it

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:44.480
Playing Domino left its mark on Beetz, quite
literally.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:48.530
She told USA Today that she has a scar on
her chest from a stray shell that hit her

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:49.850
during a shootout scene.

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:53.720
She also passed out from exhaustion, in her
leather bodysuit, in the middle of a fight

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:54.720
sequence.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:57.360
But despite it all, she says it was absolutely
worth it.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:58.360
She told RTE,

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:02.910
"We had been working so much, and I was thinking
hopefully it'll look good and I remember doing

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:07.260
the first take and then seeing the playback
and I was like, 'It's f-----g amazing!'"

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:08.260
Thanks for watching!

